      "program_name": "Inclusionary housing program and housing impact mitigation fee (studied, postponed June 9, 2026)",
      "administering_agency": "Ventura County Resource Management Agency, Planning Division",
      "funding_type": "regulatory requirement",
      "typical_award_size": "Housing Element program HE-K study by Economic and Planning Systems (funded by REAP 2.0 through the Ventura Council of Governments, September 2025) modeled a 5% moderate-income requirement on for-sale projects and 5% low-income on rentals, and a commercial linkage fee of about $4 per square foot on projects generating more than 30 employees (estimated $1.2 million over seven years). On June 9, 2026 the Board directed staff to postpone any ordinance and revisit the question in the next RHNA cycle (five to eight years), citing 225% achievement of the low-income RHNA target and minimal projected yield (about 30 units in ten years).",
