      "application_cycle": "closed/inactive",
      "next_deadline": "No action expected before the 7th cycle Housing Element (2029-2031). Cities with inclusionary programs: Oxnard, Ventura, Moorpark, Thousand Oaks, Santa Paula, Port Hueneme.",
      "prevailing_wage_trigger": "false",
      "layering_notes": "Ventura County's housing money runs through the County Executive Office, Community Development (CEO-CD, 800 S. Victoria Avenue, Ventura, (805) 654-2681), which administers the Urban County CDBG and HOME programs, the HOME Consortium, PLHA, General Fund housing NOFAs and Homekey sponsorships; the Resource Management Agency Planning Division handles density bonus, RHD zoning and streamlining; the Health Care Agency Behavioral Health holds BHSA; the Ventura County Continuum of Care (CA-611) sits in the CEO; and the Area Housing Authority of the County of Ventura (AHACV) supplies vouchers outside Oxnard, Ventura, Port Hueneme and Santa Paula, which have their own housing authorities. The nonprofit Housing Trust Fund Ventura County (HTFVC) is the de facto county revolving loan fund. The County has no inclusionary ordinance, linkage fee or dedicated housing tax. venturacounty.gov department pages block automated access, so records were built from vcportal.venturacounty.gov PDFs (Action Plan, PLHA plan, funding summaries), rma.venturacounty.gov, housingtrustfundvc.org, ahacv.org, HCD tables and press coverage. Recorded so the database shows there is no County in-lieu fee or trust fund revenue stream to pursue; the County's stated alternatives are the Prohousing Designation application (2026) and permit streamlining. Source is the Ojai Valley News report on the June 9, 2026 Board decision.",
